hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  and manga and today we have more of the  series that is black clover as we embark  on a review of the fifth arc in the  series known as the  underwater temple the very mention of  which gave me some pretty  extreme ptsd vibes in regards to every  water temple and the legend of zelda  ever however this black clover related  experience was far more enjoyable which  speaking of if you dear viewer are  finding these videos enjoyable then  kindly do the thing it is where you  subscribe to this your youtube channel  as well as like the video to let me know  that you want more black clovery stuff  as per usual i'm unlikely to be reading  the comments in this video for spoiler  reasons so that's how you let me know  but as for the underwater temple like  most black clover related stories thus  far we have quite a simple setup evil  people  are after magic stone magic stone is in  temple protagonists go to temple to get  magic stone easy done except this time  things are simplified once more because  this is essentially a black bull  exclusive story in previous arcs we've  been taking quite a bit of time to  feature other factions of the magic  knights or the diamond kingdom  but on this occasion it's pretty much  all about the bulls which i appreciated  we've been spending quite a while now  learning about them one by one so it was  very satisfying to see them all come  together as a group and just watch how  they interact with one another which was  quite shenanigan refilled  i mean i say all of them but there is  still this one apparently dude that we  have yet to meet the sort of goth  looking guy who was hardcounted by the  very concept of a beach  that's fine though it's always nice to  keep some mystery in play of course it's  not quite as simple as recovering a  miscellaneous rock though because the  temple is a pain to get into and even  when they do the squad are lured into a  game after which their game gets crashed  by the most powerful threat we face to  this point with mr midnight  cult guy so there's lots and lots to go  through but i'm going to start with noel  this arc gave her some much needed focus  because  as of late she's been a bit on the  sidelines and in fact she spent the  entirety of the last arc as comic-con  relief being all obsessed with astor and  stuff  and there's a tiny bit of that here but  it quickly shifts to surpassing her  limits a phrase which is repeated many  many many many many times during the  sock one that we've heard before but is  really cemented here but it's really  nice to see noel grow and she proved  invaluable during the course of the  underwater temple which is of course an  ideal venue for her water magic but in  addition to having a breakthrough  allowing her to take the bulls into the  temple noel is actually the first  character to get in a decent hit on our  main antagonist as well she actually has  startlingly phenomenal power which  continues to make her a nice contrast to  asta the ultimate talent in magic  standing alongside the ultimate talent  of  not magic and we also got to know a bit  more about noel as well  specifically why she was ostracized by  her family it's not just a lack of magic  control but apparently giving birth  noelle also killed the matriarch of the  family so all of her siblings despise  noel for that especially because she  can't even replace that loss by being a  classically  noble mage thing doesn't matter those  guys suck they still suck  so hard and noel has the black balls now  all of whom come to cheer her on early  on in the arc and noel repays those  bonds by standing proud at the  action-packed climax almost importantly  she has her own fuego leon moment  remembering his words about being weak  which is one of my favorite quotes i  think  ever and i really do love this because  in the last arc astor had a very similar  moment  remembering fuego leon's words to him so  these two are both growing  and it's fantastic but to talk about the  setting for a bit after noel actually  gets everyone in there the underwater  temple is indeed pretty cool but it felt  a bit underexplored to me i really like  that there was this whole civilization  down there i think that was much better  than just entering another empty temple  like the first dungeon we did but in the  end i just feel like i know  next to nothing about these guys you  know who are they why do they live down  here why can't they just go up to the  surface  they clearly have magic powerful enough  to do so so  what gives and these questions may be  answered in the future but despite the  fact that it really wasn't explored that  well in my opinion i guess  it plays into one of the overall themes  of the series being discrimination in  general either they are discriminated  against by those living on the surface  or the undersea dwellers prefer to stay  isolated for  sea dwelling reasons i don't know why  and i really do wish we'd gotten to know  a bit more about their culture because  they feel quite glossed over even our  more mainsea characters being kyoto and  kohono they had their own dreams and  tragedy but something about them just  didn't really seem to equate to the  other arc specific side characters that  we'd met up until this point the two of  them were just a bit more shallow which  is ironic given how far underwater we  were you know what doesn't really matter  though because as stated before this arc  is all about the black balls and i do  want to mention briefly just how well  thought out this scenario is from  tarpita i've mentioned this before but  he's pretty phenomenal at creating these  very natural situations like in any  other series giving such an important  mission to a band of absolute misfits  and keeping our rookie protagonists at  the forefront can be a very difficult  task  because logically there are just better  people for the job but  solves problems like these with such an  envious ease the black balls need to be  used because of the fear of a traitor  and other squads the army can't be  involved in the action because the game  would be deemed uninteresting with him  there and asta needs to be the one to  play a key role in slicing up the bad  guy because even when they know it  exists  anti-magic is still such an overpowered  x-factor in combat and so it all just  kind of works with seemingly no effort  at all meanwhile all of the effort is  seen portrayed amongst the black bulls  themselves this was such a great  showcase of teamwork with all of them  splitting off into smaller groups and  one duo that really took my eye was mana  and luck with the whole mini flashback  about the first time that mana had met  luck and how he became his first friend  and everything it was quite touching  seeing these goofballs together and even  better was that it was another emotional  realization not  triggered by astor so it felt more  natural and earned in fact that in  general was the really big selling point  to me about this arc we finally got to  see the black balls just  interact with each other absent avasta  and i love their dynamic it's such a  fascinating group to follow and another  fun combination during the arc would be  goshen grey  gray being someone who i honestly did  not remember meeting  likely because she was someone else at  the time but gray happens to have one of  my favorite magic types at the moment  though because transformation magic is  kind of like the ultimate introvert  skill set i  am truly truly envious of her ability to  just walk around as anyone she sees fit  and also it was one of those stupidly  clever combinations from tabitha with  gauche being a mirror user and gray  essentially being a reflection so i do  appreciate little thematic details like  that with that said my favorite team up  by far was the final trio of asta  vanessa and finra mostly because i never  would have predicted those two to be  such  perfect partners for astr i mean vanessa  said it best herself when she asked  how can you trust a drunk woman in a  superficial wimp with your life  and you know it's kind of true like they  were really the last two i expected to  be caught up in the ultimate battle of  the ark but they both also had their own  little flashbacks and moments and it was  just so damn good to watch these three  completely ruin veto someone who none of  these three have any business standing  up to whatsoever his power is ridiculous  and it was like watching skilled players  take down a raid boss in a game  and speaking of let's let's get to veto  i feel like i  should care about him but i don't not  yet anyway and i think that's  intentional  because after he was beaten and killed  tumba to stages this moment of respect  for vetto from yami and astor the latter  of which states that the one who felt  the most despair was obviously better so  there's this undoubtedly very sad story  behind this man that i just don't know  yet and look i say  man but that's probably wrong with all  of this mythical beast magic at play  that one was a bit of a surprise  actually and noel even recalled a story  she was told as a young member of  nobility about a race of demons and look  something tells me that whatever veto  actually was they probably weren't all  that evil that just strikes me as the  general  direction of black clover victims turn  perpetrators and all that so whilst i  still honestly don't care about veto  right now i can see a situation where we  learn of his past and the past of his  race and i look back on this and go oh  that's actually  really sad although i have to say his  obsession with despair was  well look the word despair is it's kind  of ruined for me it's honestly hard for  me to take seriously because i am a huge  huge fan of the danganronpa games where  simply saying the word despair is like  breathing oxygen so that's all i could  think of each and every time veto did so  but i did love the moment where he got  smacked in the face with the realization  right at the end that not a single  character had expressed even a shred of  despair against him in this whole  scenario  not one so suck it bad guy  who probably isn't all that bad after  all and i suppose we should move on to  asta for a bit now he's kind of always  an afterthought for me but there was one  super important moment during this arc  where we got to see that devil shadow  thing again  as well as the titular black clover  didn't get any answers regarding either  of them but  we did see them which i think is the  first time since astor received his  grimoire a boy who devours  everything even despair i'm still really  keen to know where his apparent path of  darkness takes astor because as of right  now it doesn't look like  it's had any impact on him whatsoever he  is still the epitome of optimistic and  all that is good in this world  in fact he has such a solid moral  foundation that it's almost boring and  that's what kind of weirds me out about  asta he doesn't seem to have a massive  flaw which this arc highlights actually  given that veto chastises astor for  being a hot-headed dumbass who never  gives up but then aston just turns that  on its face and basically says  na ah me being a hot-headed dumbass who  never gives up is my strongest feature  and it's just really bizarre that  despite the fact that astor is a  magicless  outcast he is still kind of perfect he  picks up non-magic related skills almost  instantly everyone loves him they're all  inspired by him most of the women want  to be with him and even his main rival  yuno treats him with the utmost respect  he's such a weird stereotypical yet  not stereotypical shonen protagonist  meanwhile yami is indeed the best as per  usual and like i said before the reason  to keep him out of most of this arc was  simple but effective high priest man  knew the game would be boring with him  involved and that's that  and i like that because characters like  yami can be very problematic yami is at  the point where he's so powerful that it  really makes no sense not to have him  involved in every serious situation so i  do hope that tabitha is good enough to  keep making these strategically  dramatically favorable decisions and  yami of course also has the best line of  the arc where he's speaking to his squad  and he just says  all of you surpassed your limits right  here and now if you die  i'll kill you that is all and hey  wouldn't you know that's what everyone  did and amongst all of that yami himself  finds a way to surpass his own limits  and we get to see him level up which was  very cool  although he does also hog all of the  glory taking down veto single-handedly  after the amazing effort put in by the  rest of the squad but you know i'm okay  with that because it's yami oh and  something else involving yami tambita  seems to have gone to some great lengths  in this arc to make it very clear that  the magic knight ranking system is not  to be equated with power which yes we  did already know however it gets spelled  out to us pretty clearly with all the  other black balls being junior magic  knights apparently who then go on to  fight very well against the equivalent  of intermediate and  even senior ranks and that also gets  taken a step further when those juniors  also combine to take on the main  antagonist who is either on or above the  level of a captain  so ranking wanking whatever doesn't  matter all i know is that i want more  charmy she was absolutely  robbed in this arc and needs more action  immediately but other than that another  very nice arc from black clover i should  also add that the black balls got  thanked at the end which was a new  experience for them as they are  generally looked down upon outcast so  that was all  nice and new but that pretty much does  it for this blind review of the  underwater temple arc of black clover  and what do you guys think please do  leave your thoughts in the comments  below or even join my discord server and  if you're keen for more black clover  content then please do go and check out  some of my other videos or even  subscribe to the channel for  very maybe regular black clover goodness  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review  and i'll see you next time

